{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Lot went with him.</b> Because his father Haran died in Ur of the Chaldees on account of his brother Abraham, as our Rabbis said, Lot was like a member of his household." "<b>And Abram was seventy-five years old.</b> Scripture counts his years, to teach that his father was still alive." "<b>When he went out from Haran.</b> A second time, as is stated in Seder Olam: he returned to Haran and stayed there five years, as it is written: ״ואברם בן חמש שנים ושבעים שנה בצאתו מחרן״ (and Abram was seventy-five years old when he went out from Haran)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:57.670680410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}